                <pb facs="0210" n="106" xml:id="pg106"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mizner to Mr.
                            Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1890-09-21"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 21,
                        1890</date>. (City of Mexico, September 21, 1890.)</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Ryan states that a telegram from Minister Mizner asks him to telegraph the
                    Department that peace and order reign in Guatemala, and that his (Mr. Mizner’s)
                    next dispatch will conclude the history of the case of General Barrundia.</p>
            </div>
